  "data": {
    "body": "Consider a simply supported beam of length L with a force P applied at x = L/2, as shown in the figure below. The elastic modulus is E and the cross-sectional moment of inertia is I.\n\na) Use Castigliano\u2019s theorem to find the downward deflection at x = L/2. \n\nb) Without performing any calculations, describe in words how you would find the deflection of the above beam at x = L/4 using Castigliano\u2019s theorem. Write no more than three complete sentences.",
    "solution": "a) $\\frac{PL^3}{48EI}$",
